Files: whistle/whistle.cact
       whistle/libneedle3.so
       whistle/wrapper.whl
Copyright: Cactus Compute
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: Not in the source tree: the offline writing-down artifacts are
 fetched at build time from the URLs pinned, with their sha256, in
 whistle/pins.json, checked, and installed unmodified (never stripped) in
 /usr/share/cassini-viewer/whistle. whistle.cact holds the Whistle speech
 recognition weights; libneedle3.so is the Needle 3.3.0 engine, taken from
 its pinned wheel; wrapper.whl is the cactus-needle 3.2.0 Python wrapper.
 Sources: https://huggingface.co/Cactus-Compute/whistle,
 https://huggingface.co/Cactus-Compute/needle3 and
 https://github.com/cactus-compute/needle. See whistle/NOTICE.md.

Files: whistle/silero_vad.onnx
Copyright: 2020-present Silero Team
License: MIT
Comment: Not in the source tree: Silero VAD v6.2.1, from
 https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad at the revision pinned, with its
 sha256, in whistle/pins.json; fetched at build time and installed
 unmodified in /usr/share/cassini-viewer/whistle.

Files: onnxruntime/*
Copyright: Microsoft Corporation
License: MIT
Comment: Not in the source tree: ONNX Runtime 1.31.0, the PyPI wheel for the
 package's Python, fetched at build time from the URL pinned, with its
 sha256, in whistle/pins.json, and installed unpacked and unmodified (never
 stripped) in /usr/lib/<multiarch>/cassini-viewer/python, without its
 transformers, quantization, tools and backend subpackages or its C API
 library.
 The extension module includes third-party components under their own
 licences; onnxruntime/ThirdPartyNotices.txt, installed with it, lists them.
 Source: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

